    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <mrow>
        <mi>T</mi>
        <mo>=</mo>
        <mn>0</mn>
        <mspace width="0.2em"></mspace>
        <mtext>K</mtext>
      </mrow>
    </annotation-xml>
  </semantics>
</math> for Various Superconductors</span>

  <span class="os-divider"> </span>
</div>
</div>
<p id="fs-id1172102078852">Type II superconductors are generally compounds or alloys involving transition metals or actinide series elements. Almost all superconductors with relatively high critical temperatures are type II. They have two critical fields, represented by <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><m